{
  "_doc": "The T2T consortium's v2.0 analysis sets with the acrocentric short arms' distal junctions, rDNA arrays and pseudo-homologous regions hard-masked (layer_t2t_dj_rdna_phr), and the chr1 5S rDNA array too in the _5S sets (layer_t2t_5s_rdna); chrY masked whole for XX samples (layer_chry), at its PARs for XY (layer_par_y), or, in the _noY sets, all but its first base (layer_chry_from_2: an off-by-one, reproduced). rCRS as chrM in the forXX, forXY and _wi_rCRS sets; CHM13's own mitochondrion in the other two _5S sets. No file publishes the masked spans: the layers are read from the sets themselves (book.toml derived_masks).",
